    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense, but I've been seeing a lot of debate online about it. Some people argue that sex is the more fundamental biological reality and that identity shouldn't be separated from it. How does the scientific community respond to those specific criticisms? Is there any actual scientific basis to the idea that they are essentially the same thing?",
